# Template for a Google-managed Agent Gateway in "Client-to-Agent" (ingress)
# mode - it sits in front of the deployed agent and governs/inspects
# incoming client requests (e.g. calls to reasoningEngines.query) before
# they reach Agent Runtime.
#
# Unlike the egress gateway, this one does NOT reference Agent Registry -
# the registry isn't used for ingress - and it MUST be created in the same
# project and region as the agent (egress gateways may live in a different
# project, as long as the region matches).
#
# Render with envsubst before importing, e.g.:
#   AGW_NAME=mcp-agent-gateway-ingress envsubst \
#     < deploy/templates/ingress_gateway.yaml.tmpl > rendered.yaml
#
# Reference: https://docs.cloud.google.com/gemini-enterprise-agent-platform/govern/gateways/set-up-agent-gateway
#
# On `protocols: [MCP]` below: this traffic (a client calling
# reasoningEngines.query) is obviously not MCP wire protocol. It's set to
# MCP anyway because, per someone who reverse-engineered the actual JSON
# schema (the import validator echoes its full schema back on a rejected
# document), `protocols` currently accepts only two enum values for the
# whole Agent Gateway resource type - MCP and PROTOCOL_UNSPECIFIED - with
# no distinct value yet for agent-query/A2A-style traffic:
# https://dev.to/iamrobertmoore/five-things-i-found-in-googles-agent-registry-and-agent-gateway-that-arent-in-the-docs-236f
# This is a real rough edge on a brand-new (2026) surface, not a
# deliberate choice on our part. To get 100% ground truth yourself, submit
# an intentionally-invalid value (e.g. `protocols: [BOGUS]`) with
# setup_ingress_gateway.sh - the rejected import prints the live schema.

name: ${AGW_NAME}
protocols:
  - MCP
googleManaged:
  governedAccessPath: CLIENT_TO_AGENT
